    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion and kind words!\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, incremental search is meant to be as quick as possible. Thus it does not seem to trigger any events which 'mini.animate' can \"hook\" into (like `CursorMoved` currently used for animating cursor movement). See [this comment](https://github.com/vim/vim/issues/11628#issuecomment-1328220365) for reference as well as the whole issue discussion. Thus I am afraid it is not really possible to do that right now. And if it *is* made possible, then `CursorMoved` would trigger right away making cursor animated.\r\n\r\nClosing as \"not possible at the moment and if made possible should work out of the box\".",
            "created_at": "2024-06-05T12:50:25Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/945#issuecomment-2149779486",
